//! Data access over sqlx for the `repository` generator's crates: a table described as data,
//! the list query (the nine filter operators, sort and paging), and the reads and writes on
//! Postgres and SQLite.
//!
//! A row is read into the JSON a model type deserializes from, and a body a caller sends is
//! serialized to JSON and bound column by column, so the model types stay free of sqlx and a
//! store crate is a table descriptor and a few typed functions over this one.
//!
//! The wire forms are the ones every port's runtime reads and writes
//! (`fixtures/persistence-conformance/normalization.md`): on SQLite a boolean is `0`/`1`, a
//! duration is its length in microseconds, a JSON value and an array are JSON text, and a
//! timestamp is the text the caller sent. A null sorts after every value (ascending) and
//! before every value (descending) on both engines.

